<!--Blurb: What is your best wealth?-->
<h2 class="h1">Wealth<br/>
Vitta Sutta  (SN 1:73)</h2>
<div class="verse">
<pre>“What is a person’s best wealth here?
What, well practiced, brings bliss?
What’s the most excellent of savors?
Living in what way
	is one’s life called the best?”</pre>
<pre>“Conviction is a person’s best wealth here.
Dhamma, well practiced, brings bliss.
Truth is the most excellent of savors.
Living with discernment,
	one’s life is called best.”</pre>
</div><!--end verse-->
<p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../AN/AN7_6.html" class="sutta-ref">AN 7:6–7</a>; <a href="../KN/StNp/StNp1_10.html" class="sutta-ref">Sn 1:10</a></p>

      </div><!--end:sutta-->
